# Tracer: nested forall, arithmetic, and exact WD occurrence replay.
#
# Before (Litex verified, To-Lean did not compile):
# forall f fn(x R) R:
#     forall y R:
#         f(y) = f(y - 1)
#     =>:
#         f(2) = f(1)
# Former To-Lean behavior: nested `forall` facts were not rendered, `y - 1`
# had no universal-object operation, and applications selected WD evidence by
# structural object text rather than one exact source occurrence.
#
# Now (verified and compiled by the focused Rust/Mathlib gates):
forall f fn(x R) R:
    forall y R:
        f(y) = f(y - 1)
    =>:
        f(2) = f(1)
# Current behavior: `y` remains a LitexObject, `Litex.sub` models subtraction,
# `realSubClosure` replays the verifier's operand-membership certificate, and
# every `f(...)` consumes the WD fact attached to its source occurrence ID.
#
# Boundary: a target requirement whose occurrence ID is missing or changed is
# rejected; the emitter does not fall back to proposition or object-text search.
# Source gate:
# target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/05_compiler_interop/compile_to_lean_arithmetic_forall_wd.lit
# Focused compiler gate:
# cargo test --release arithmetic_forall_tracer_replays_subtraction_and_well_definedness -- --nocapture
# Real Lean gate:
# LITEX_LEAN_PROJECT=/absolute/path/to/mathlib LITEX_LAKE=/absolute/path/to/lake cargo test --release arithmetic_forall_tracer_compiles_with_mathlib -- --ignored --nocapture
